WEBVTT

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:07.870
Narumi.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.380
This is the last of the Aqua Vitae.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:16.090
The first symbol of alchemy.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:20.510
Rise like a phoenix
with this supreme medicine.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.720
And give me your assistance.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.070
Before dawn, when the stars paint the sky

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:44.030
I am searching for the thing I lost

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.700
With a restless heart
Under the sun yet in the dark

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:53.290
I patch together little prayers
to light my path

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:57.960
I don't need anything,
as my hands are full

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:02.970
My hands are full of emptiness

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:07.720
Please, just once, nod for me

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:12.480
Just once, reach out to me like the mirror

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:17.360
I will live for that single moment,
that single second

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.780
All the rest can just burn away

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.870
What's right for me is for me alone

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:32.000
Whatever the path, I'll follow it to you

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:36.460
This feeling grows and grows,
deep inside my heart

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:39.920
For one single reason

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:47.970
I continue to climb up on the stage

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:00.780
#6 Hell

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:05.150
Why? Why am
I fighting?

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.280
I woke up from a long sleep
one month ago.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:17.710
While asleep,
I kept seeing the same dream.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.590
A crying girl.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:24.090
And a kid with a great smile.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:29.180
But I couldn't tell who they were.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.310
Nor who I was.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.100
I had lost my memory.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.230
You're finally awake.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:44.150
How do you feel?

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:49.410
You were hurt pretty badly,

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.240
so I guess you don't feel so great yet.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.330
Where am I?

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:57.870
A hospital in Illinois in the US.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:02:59.920
The US?

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.920
A hospital...

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.170
Why?

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.050
But more than that...

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.220
who in the world am I?

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:14.140
It seems like you've lost your memory.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:16.600
Along with your arm.

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:23.150
According to your driver's license,
your name is Narumi Kato.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.530
Narumi... Kato?

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.570
I can't remember anything.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.120
Don't worry.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:36.580
It's not unusual to have temporary
memory loss after a big accident.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.500
Let me introduce myself.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:43.040
I'm a descendant of French aristocracy

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:48.010
and connoisseur of all that's beautiful.
My name is Guy Christophe Rech.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:53.970
That old lady who looks like a witch
out of a fairytale is Lucille Verneuil.

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:55.930
That analogy was unnecessary.

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:59.020
Why did I lose my arm?

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:01.310
Because of this "big accident"?

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:04.480
Oh, good. You've come around.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:07.740
-I'll go get Dr. Banhart...
-Miss Helen.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.570
How beautiful you are,
any time of the day.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.820
Like a bouquet of roses.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:14.700
But we just met...

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:16.620
Guy, was it?

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:21.620
Don't go around hitting on girls
when I'm talking to you.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:25.500
Quite lively for a man
who's just awakened.

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:31.340
Maman, a brute from Japan
is bullying me.

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:33.510
Who are you calling a brute!

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:41.730
Calm down, I'll explain everything.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:43.440
When I found you...

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:45.150
Wait, we'll talk later.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.610
Hey, wait!

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.450
I'm not...

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:03.500
I just...

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.590
What the heck am I doing?

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:18.100
It's like my body has a mind of its own.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:22.140
Why am I doing martial arts
in front of these kids?

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:24.900
Martial arts?

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:28.400
That's it, I remember.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:31.900
I've learned martial arts in China before.

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:34.740
-That's so cool!
-Wow.

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:37.700
What was that?

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.540
Show us again!

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.010
That's... No!

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:57.510
Are you okay, Mark?
I'm so happy you're here with us.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.940
ZONAPHA syndrome?

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:19.910
Don't be so reckless.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:24.460
You've just recovered from injuries
that almost took your life.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:32.340
I don't know the details, but you were
in an explosion at a mansion in Japan.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:35.720
By the time I arrived,
you'd almost lost too much blood.

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:42.640
So I brought you to this state-of-the-art
hospital to save you.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:46.350
That kid.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:47.850
Yes, Mark.

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:52.730
He has ZONAPHA syndrome, right?

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:58.110
I remembered that I have the same illness.

00:06:58.490 --> 00:06:59.450
That's right.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:04.950
Around 2,000 children with ZONAPHA
syndrome are cared for at this center.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:09.460
It's the world's leading
ZONAPHA research and treatment facility.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.460
2,000 kids...

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:15.630
He's sufficiently recovered.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.340
He can go to some other hospital now.

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:23.350
Why don't you all leave already,
Mr. Guy and Ms. Lucille?

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:25.850
-Why?
-You're asking us why?

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:30.980
You know why. We don't exactly like you.

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:35.110
The disease is spreading because
you're taking too long to stop it.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:40.740
Then why don't you hurry up
and find a way to cure it?

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:43.780
-Who are you to say that!
-Stop it, Peter.

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:50.080
Ms. Lucille is here to gather information
from the children.

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:57.470
But I am with you in hoping
she hurries up and finishes her job here.

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:02.680
There's still a lot I don't get.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:07.520
But thanks. You saved my life.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:12.810
Why though? Why bring me
all the way to the US to save me?

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:16.440
Did I know you?

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:18.490
No, we'd never met.

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:22.320
I was in Japan to scout you.

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:24.280
Scout? What for?

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:26.080
You'll see in time.

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:31.040
For now, focus on regaining your strength.

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:38.710
Still clueless about what was going on,
my life at the hospital began.

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:42.720
My job was to sleep well, eat well...

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.600
and play with the kids.

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:52.100
This prosthetic arm is incredible.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:54.650
It moves like the real thing.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:59.320
I'd lost my memory, but not my feelings.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:05.320
I loved the kids,
and they became attached to me.

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:07.660
Here Beth, an elephant.

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:10.790
That doesn't look like an elephant.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:16.840
Can I have that, Narumi?
I'm collecting everyone's pictures.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.460
You sure? It's a pretty crummy drawing.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:25.680
Pictures remind me
of the people who drew them.

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:28.930
So I can remember those people forever.

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:30.560
Narumi.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:32.690
Draw me a gorilla.

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:35.730
A gorilla? One that looks like this?

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:44.360
Phew, I'm pooped.
Those little scamps are bundles of energy.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:48.280
That sweet Mark,
holding onto my drawing like that.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:53.080
Tom is usually quiet, but he gets
fired up when it comes to soccer.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:56.380
And Beth likes dressing up.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:07.970
Nurse Helen?

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:20.190
What the... Vitamins or something?

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:49.260
Hey! All your doctors and nurses
are getting high on drugs.

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:51.970
They can't treat ZONAPHA patients
like that!

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:57.190
So what? It's necessary for them
to do their jobs.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:11:00.230
That's how it is. Now get out.

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:06.570
So you saw it, didn't you?

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:08.610
The Midnight Circus.

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:13.620
Tom! Hey, what's going on?

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:16.000
Treating kids like criminals!

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:21.960
Ruthlessly interrogating
children whose parents were killed

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:23.960
is part of hunting the automata.

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:26.090
That is their job.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:31.470
You have no time to be scared.
You're about to die.

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:35.180
Don't you want to be of help
before you do?

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:39.650
Guy, you bastard!

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:50.200
You heartless wretch.
Think about the kids' feelings!

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:54.740
Dear me. The brute has quite a temper.

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:59.370
You too! High on drugs,
and you call yourselves doctors?

00:12:16.140 --> 00:12:17.140
Narumi.

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:23.900
You think the kids here don't have
so many attacks because we treat them?

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:25.980
That's not it.

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:29.740
ZONAPHA is full of mysteries.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:32.450
There's only one thing we can do.

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:35.330
It's to smile for the children.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:40.410
To do that, the entire staff here
force ourselves to smile.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:43.750
We relax the parasympathetic
nervous system.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:46.000
With drugs?

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:49.090
You force yourselves to smile?

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:53.050
The only way to ease an attack
is to make someone smile.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:57.470
So what else can we do but smile?

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:02.060
The research isn't going so well,
and it makes us anxious.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:07.020
But we can't let
our negative feelings show.

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:09.030
We just can't...

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:11.490
However painful...

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:14.110
No...

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:18.790
It seems like you need to know the truth.

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:21.620
May I, Dr. Banhart?

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.960
Narumi, this hospital,

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:31.380
it's hell.

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:40.810
Nice weather today, Anselmus.

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:45.480
Yes, Paulmann.
Perfect weather for killing a shirogane.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:49.020
Guy, a legendary European shirogane.

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:52.400
Let's present to Lady Francine
his head on a stick.

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:57.070
I'm thirsty for human blood, too.

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:02.700
The Intensive Care Unit?

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:07.500
There are 3 stages to ZONAPHA syndrome.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:11.880
The first is breathing difficulties
and pain all over.

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:15.590
The second is complications
due to immune deficiencies.

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:19.010
Most don't make it past this stage.

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:27.480
Mark!

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:29.770
Hang in there, Mark!

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:33.530
Why? You were fine just a while ago.

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:35.820
Don't, we're treating him now.

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:40.620
But those who die might be the lucky ones.

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:43.450
What do you mean by that?

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:47.710
The true horror of ZONAPHA
lies in the final stage.

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:49.460
Simply put...

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:54.010
they can't die anymore.

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:19.620
Do you think this is cruel?

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:24.580
Their body temperatures have dropped
and their muscles are rigid.

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:27.160
Beds are useless.

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.880
Do you get it now?

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:37.130
Why this hospital is a living hell.

00:15:39.340 --> 00:15:42.180
Tell me one thing.

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:45.600
What did you do to me?

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:49.100
My hand healed itself.

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:51.360
Come to think of it,

00:15:52.270 --> 00:15:55.190
I went through an accident
that cost me an arm.

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:58.200
I shouldn't be this healed
in just 2 months.

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:01.240
So you finally realized.

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:06.160
I used Aqua Vitae.

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:09.290
To save you.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:11.250
Aqua Vitae?

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:16.260
It's an elixir that can cure anything.

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:19.220
Then maybe...

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:22.220
Yes, ZONAPHA too.

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:27.600
Indeed, it's the only way
to cure ZONAPHA syndrome.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:29.430
Then why...?

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:33.190
It's all gone. We used it up on you.

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:39.190
An ancient alchemist made the Aqua Vitae.

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:41.780
We cannot recreate it.

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:44.410
I don't get it. Why?

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:48.370
If what you're saying is true,
why did you use it on me?

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:51.080
You could've saved the kids.

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:55.960
There was only a small quantity left.
Far from enough to save them all.

00:16:56.130 --> 00:16:59.420
But you could've saved at least a few.

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:03.550
I told you I was in Japan to scout you.

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:07.100
Narumi, assist me in my work.

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:09.310
To defeat the automata.

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:11.140
Automata?

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:16.230
ZONAPHA syndrome is cloaked in mystery.

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:19.320
But we know where it comes from.

00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:23.360
It's being spread by the automata.

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:29.240
And the group commanding them
is the Midnight Circus.

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:53.270
Our mission is to crush them.

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:56.770
Narumi, I need you to become a shirogane.

00:17:58.980 --> 00:18:01.280
Shi-Shirogane?

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:05.200
What's wrong?

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:07.870
I... Nothing.

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:10.330
They're here.

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:15.250
They've come for our lives
and human blood.

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:17.580
It's Paulmann and Anselmus.

00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:35.850
The humans have learned nothing,
have they Paulmann?

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:37.560
Seems not, Anselmus.

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:40.650
Weapons are no use against us.

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:42.690
Take them somewhere safe!

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:45.740
-Narumi, I'm scared.
-Don't worry, I'm here.

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:53.410
You must be Guy.

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:55.120
You're mine.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:58.540
Nice to meet you. And goodbye.

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:01.420
Olympia.

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:14.720
That's what Guy can do.

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:18.850
All the shirogane use puppets
to defeat the automata.

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:21.480
Those are the automata?

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:26.440
Lucille, is it true that they're the ones
spreading the disease?

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:32.330
Yes. Which is why we must defeat them.

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:42.290
Beth, is it an attack? Hold on!
I'll take you to the treatment room.

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:45.800
Narumi, will you do something for me?

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:46.800
What?

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:50.720
Your gorilla face...

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:54.310
it was really funny.

00:19:55.390 --> 00:19:58.730
Will you do it again for me?

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:23.460
Damn it...

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:29.010
I'm the one
that's supposed to laugh for her...

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:33.430
Not the other way around.

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:36.310
Why, Guy?

00:20:37.140 --> 00:20:40.440
Why did you use the Aqua Vitae on me?

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:42.650
You heard Guy.

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:49.400
Saving a couple of children with
what was left of it would solve nothing.

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:53.990
Instead, if you become a shirogane
and defeat the automata,

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:57.790
we'll be able to save
a far greater number.

00:20:58.580 --> 00:20:59.910
Yeah...

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:02.540
Yeah but...

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:05.920
Would you like to wear this?

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:09.340
A mask?

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:13.220
An alchemist once wore it long ago.

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:16.430
He had gone through bitter times.

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:18.770
This is what I believe.

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:25.230
When reality is too harsh, we need
to hide something in order to face it.

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:28.610
A mask will hide one's broken heart.

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:39.490
You're just a measly human!

00:21:49.550 --> 00:21:50.670
That's it, Narumi!

00:21:55.510 --> 00:21:57.720
That's why I scouted you.

00:21:59.430 --> 00:22:01.390
When hit with spiritual force,

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:04.940
automata's fluids oscillate
to the point of explosion.

00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:09.020
Let me do the rest, Guy.

00:22:14.610 --> 00:22:16.950
Fly up high, Marionette

00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:19.200
Turn to ash, gracefully

00:22:19.370 --> 00:22:23.750
My only purpose in life was to fight

00:22:23.910 --> 00:22:28.540
Why am I so angry
even I dump my humanity

00:22:28.710 --> 00:22:34.880
Without you, I can't smile anymore

00:22:35.930 --> 00:22:40.140
I assume that I am to be blamed

00:22:40.310 --> 00:22:44.640
Like a puppet that can't smile naturally

00:22:44.810 --> 00:22:49.770
I feel like someone is pulling my strings

00:22:49.940 --> 00:22:53.440
What am I even living for?

00:22:53.610 --> 00:22:57.780
I was hurt, and thought
that nobody would understand

00:22:57.950 --> 00:23:02.910
But you came along,
and took me in your arms

00:23:03.080 --> 00:23:09.080
I felt my tangled arms and legs

00:23:09.460 --> 00:23:11.460
become free

00:23:11.670 --> 00:23:13.960
Fly up high, Marionette

00:23:14.130 --> 00:23:16.380
I think now I can reach you

00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:20.850
Before I met you, I was empty

00:23:21.010 --> 00:23:25.770
Now I have something
I'd give my all to protect

00:23:25.930 --> 00:23:32.150
You taught me how to feel,
the feeling of sorrow too
